english_question:
If the three views of a certain spatial geometric body are as shown in the figure, then the volume of this geometric body is ( )
A. \frac{1}{3}
B. \frac{2}{3}
C. 1
D. 2

The figure is a planar development of a geometric body, where ABCD is a square, and E and F are the midpoints of PA and PD, respectively. In this geometric body, the following four conclusions are given: 
① Line BE is skew to line CF; 
② Line BE is skew to line AF; 
③ Line EF is parallel to plane PBC; 
④ Plane BCE is perpendicular to plane PAD. 
How many of the statements are correct?

In the figure, there are two squares with a side length of 2. The vertex O of square OPQR is the center of square ABCD. The following conclusions are given: 
1. The area of quadrilateral OECF = 1; 
2. EC + CF = 2; 
3. EO + OF = 2; 
4. The perimeter of quadrilateral OECF = 4. 
Which of the above conclusions are correct? ( )
A. 1 2 3 4
B. 1 2
C. 1 3
D. 1 4

In the figure, ∠MON=90°, OB=2, point A is a moving point on line OM, connect AB, and construct the angle bisectors AF and BF of ∠MAB and ∠ABN, respectively. The lines of the two angle bisectors intersect at point F. Find the minimum value of segment BF as point A moves.
A. 2
B. \sqrt { 2 }
C. 4
D. \sqrt { 3 }

The image shows the net of a cube. In this cube, 
(1) BM and ED are skew lines; 
(2) CN is parallel to BE; 
(3) CN forms a 60-degree angle with BM; 
(4) DM is perpendicular to BN. 
Among the four statements above, the correct statement numbers are ( )
A. (1)(2)(3)(4)
B. (2)(4)
C. (2)(3)(4)
D. (2)(3)

As shown in the figure, point P is a moving point on the edge AA<sub>1</sub> of the triangular prism ABC-A<sub>1</sub>B<sub>1</sub>C<sub>1</sub>. If the volume of the tetrahedron P-BCC<sub>1</sub>B<sub>1</sub> is V, then the volume of the triangular prism ABC-A<sub>1</sub>B<sub>1</sub>C<sub>1</sub> is ( )
A. 2V
B. 3V
C. \frac {4V}{3}
D. \frac {3V}{2}

In the figure, PA and PB are two tangents to circle O, with points A and B as the points of tangency. The line OP intersects circle O at points C and D, and intersects line AB at point E. AF is the diameter of circle O. The following conclusions are given: 
1) ∠ABP = ∠AOP; 
2) $\widehat{\bar{B}C}$ = $\widehat{F D}$; 
3) AC bisects ∠PAB; 
4) 2BE<sup>2</sup> = PE • BF. 
Which of the conclusions are correct? ( )
A. 1
B. 2
C. 3
D. 4

In the right triangle ABC, where AB = AC = 4, a circle with diameter AB intersects BC at point D. What is the area of the shaded region?
A. 3 - \frac{\pi}{2}
B. 3 - \pi
C. 6 - \pi
D. 6 - \frac{\pi}{2}
